%I A401305 #26 Nov 22 2026 12:33:26
%S A401305 5,13,61,109,421,1621,5149,8941,13381,62269,148261,300301,644869,
%T A401305 644869,3249541,3462229,6810301,16145221,39136549,43030381,163384621,
%U A401305 249623581,1169755141,1169755141,2055693949,5959962661,5959962661,7209891781,30116328181,81819444589,205347072709
%N A401305 Least number congruent to 5 modulo 8 that is a quadratic residue modulo the first n odd primes.
%C A401305 Let N = A102476(n+2) be the least modulus with 2^(n+2) square roots of 1. a(n) is the minimal element of the coset of (Z/NZ)*^2 in (Z/NZ)* containing A402499(n+1) = N/2 + 1, or the least m coprime to N such that A402499(n+1)/m is a square modulo N. Here (Z/NZ)* is the multiplicative group of integers modulo N and (Z/NZ)*^2 is the subgroup of squares.
%C A401305 For each n, while a(n) is a square in R and in Q_p for 3 <= p <= prime(n+1), Q_2 is a witness of a(n) being a nonsquare (i.e., a(n) is not a (local) square in Q_2). Similar constructions:
%C A401305   -A045535(n) < 0 is a square in Q_p for 2 <= p <= prime(n+1) but not in R;
%C A401305   A401356(n) == 2 (mod 3) is a square in R, Q_2, and in Q_p for 5 <= p <= prime(n+1) but not in Q_3;
%C A401305   A402507(n) == 7 (mod 8) is a square in R and in Q_p for 3 <= p <= prime(n+1) but not in Q_2;
%C A401305   A402547(n) == 3 (mod 8) is a square in R and in Q_p for 3 <= p <= prime(n+1) but not in Q_2.
%C A401305 For any fundamental discriminant D of a quadratic field dividing N, kronecker(D,a(n)) = -1 if and only if 8 divides D.
%e A401305 The cosets of (Z/NZ)*^2 in (Z/NZ)* containing A402499(n+1) = N/2 + 1, with N = A102476(n+2) for n=0..4:
%e A401305   {5}
%e A401305   {13}
%e A401305   {61, 109}
%e A401305   {109, 421, 541, 589, 709, 781}
%e A401305   {421, 709, 949, 1549, 1621, 2269, 2941, 3061, 3301, 3469, 4141, 4621, 4789, 4909, 4981, 5149, 5461, 5581, 5989, 6301, 6469, 6829, 7261, 7309, 7429, 8101, 8149, 8341, 8941, 9109}
%o A401305 (PARI) A401305(n, st=5) = my(P = prime(n+1)); forstep(k=st, oo, 8, forprime(p=3, P, if(kronecker(k, p)<1, next(2))); return(k)) \\ st == 5 (mod 8) allows to calculate a(n) if a(n-1) is known
%Y A401305 Cf. A102476. See A402499 for a list of related sequences.
%K A401305 nonn,new
%O A401305 0,1
%A A401305 _Jianing Song_, Nov 20 2026
